    """
    A Least Recently Used (LRU) cache implementation.

    This cache stores a limited number of key-value pairs. When the cache
    reaches its capacity, the least recently used item is evicted to make
    room for new entries. Access to items is O(1) on average, and updates
    are also O(1) on average.

